3. R-8 DETECTION (mesh_analysis.py — decompose_mesh_faces)

Insertion point: AFTER the face construction loop (after line 2299, before
curved patches extraction).  AFTER all per-face warnings are computed from
_count_residual_loop_edges (L2278-2279), so the total unpaired count is
deterministic.

Residual-edge source (same as R-4 per-face warnings):
  unpaired_total = sum(face["warnings"][0]["count"]
                       for face in planar_faces if face.get("warnings"))

This is the SAME source R-4 uses at L2278-2284: _count_residual_loop_edges
counts how many residual_pairs from _boundary_loops appear as consecutive
vertex pairs in the final face loops.  Every residual_pair corresponds to a
non-manifold edge with |net| >= 2 in _boundary_loops' edge cancellation.

Ratio formula:
  ratio = unpaired_total / (3 * len(welded_tris))
  where welded_tris is the welded triangle count (post _weld_vertices)

Threshold: > 5% (0.05).  When triggered, TWO new keys in return dict:
  "strategy_fallback_suggested": "organic"
  "unpaired_pct": round(100.0 * unpaired_total / (3 * n_welded_tris), 1)

When NOT triggered, NO new keys appear — the return dict is byte-identical
to pre-R-8 output for existing tests.

The empty-input early-return path (L2097-2099) is unchanged: its hardcoded
dict never includes the new keys.

Wire-up to return dict: changed from inline dict literal to named variable
(result) so keys can be conditionally added before return.

