7. T11 WELD-REORDER ARTIFACT (design decision)

T11 learnings document that the weld's rounded-key grid can reorder vertex
indices, creating INTERMEDIATE non-manifold edges in _boundary_loops'
residual_pairs even on a clean mesh.  The 5% threshold is the guard against
this: a watertight box produces zero post-pinch residuals (loop-chaining
handles the intermediates), so the ratio stays at 0.0.  Even if a specific
weld order produced a few spurious residuals, they'd be far below 5%.

The clean-mesh test explicitly asserts strategy_fallback_suggested NOT in
result, confirming the threshold works against this artifact.
